{
  "slug": "vibe-flow",
  "name": "Vibe Flow",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Orchestration skills for Vibe Kanban. Turn a spec into merged code using multi-agent waves: plan → ship → link → review → merge, with autonomous fix loops. Supports parallel wave dispatch, executor tier routing (T0 flash → T4 opus), board status transitions, and cost budgets.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills** and **2 agents**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `vibe-dispatch-fix` (Use when a PR failed review or CI - re-dispatches a workspace to fix the critical/important review items…), `vibe-export-kanban` (Use after the final vibe-ship-fast PR has merged to sync results back to vibe-kanban - posts a comment…), `vibe-flow` (Use when you have a spec or set of requirements and want the full end-to-end loop from spec…), `vibe-import-kanban` (Use when you want to ship existing vibe-kanban issues locally with vibe-ship-fast - pulls issues from a vibe-kanban…), `vibe-init` (Use on first-time setup in a new repo - picks the vibe-kanban project via MCP, writes a minimal…), `vibe-link` (Use when a workspace finished and pushed a branch - finds or creates the corresponding GitHub PR, links…), `vibe-merge` (Use when a PR is approved by vibe-review and ready to merge - verifies CI green, checks for…), `vibe-plan` (Use when you have a spec, feature request, or set of requirements that needs to be broken into…), and 6 more\n- **Agents** (2): `vibe-explorer` (Fresh subagent that explores the codebase and proposes ONE approach to a problem through a specific lens (simplicity/performance/extensibility)), `vibe-reviewer` (Fresh subagent that performs two-stage code review (spec compliance then code quality) on a GitHub PR)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install vibe-flow@claude-community` from `OAI-Labs/vibe-flow` (`plugins/vibe-flow`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 14,
    "agent": 2
  },
